  "ssml": "<speak version=\"1.0\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis\" xmlns:mstts=\"https://www.w3.org/2001/mstts\" xml:lang=\"en-PH\">\n  <voice name=\"en-PH-RosaNeural\">\n    <mstts:express-as style=\"friendly\">\n      <prosody rate=\"96%\" pitch=\"+2%\">\n        Welcome to <emphasis level=\"moderate\">San Victor Island</emphasis>! <break time=\"550ms\"/> Let&apos;s look at this puzzle together. <break time=\"550ms\"/> When you see <emphasis level=\"moderate\">Night</emphasis> is to <emphasis level=\"moderate\">Day</emphasis>, <break time=\"300ms\"/> as <emphasis level=\"moderate\">Happy</emphasis> is to <emphasis level=\"moderate\">Sad</emphasis>, <break time=\"300ms\"/> here&apos;s how we read it out loud: <emphasis level=\"moderate\">Night</emphasis> is to <emphasis level=\"moderate\">Day</emphasis>, <break time=\"300ms\"/> as <emphasis level=\"moderate\">Happy</emphasis> is to <emphasis level=\"moderate\">Sad</emphasis>. <break time=\"550ms\"/> Notice the pattern? <break time=\"650ms\"/> <break time=\"800ms\"/> <emphasis level=\"moderate\">Night</emphasis> and <emphasis level=\"moderate\">Day</emphasis> are <emphasis level=\"moderate\">opposites</emphasis>! <break time=\"550ms\"/> That means our bridge relationship is <emphasis level=\"moderate\">Antonyms</emphasis>.\n      </prosody>\n    </mstts:express-as>\n  </voice>\n</speak>",
